 
          <p>Boo! Happy Halloween. See you next year for another scare. In the meantime, life slogs, and sometimes rushes, on. We&rsquo;ve had the pleasure to experience the grand opening of the flu season resulting in more sleep deprivation whilst trying to take care of the sick kids. As you can imagine, dodging sickness itself became an impossible task. It looks like every month comes with something to complain about.</p>
<p>Did you know that nonstick pans only last two to five years, according to the shop assistant that talked me into buying two new ones? The Teflon layer got nicked (and consumed??) so this time I went with a hardened ceramic layer. After taking care of the bill, I said &ldquo;see you in ten years then&rdquo;, to which he replied &ldquo;no&rdquo;. I guess I&rsquo;ll be extra careful this time.</p>
<p>Previous month: <a href="/post/2026/10/september-2026/">September 2026</a>.</p>
<h2 id="games-ive-played">Games I&rsquo;ve played</h2>
<p>This month mostly represented clearing out the <em>Castlevania</em>-related backlog:</p>
<ul>
<li>I replayed <a href="https://jefklakscodex.com/games/ds/castlevania-order-of-ecclesia/">Order of Ecclesia</a> 18 years after playing it for the first time. It still rocks, but I&rsquo;ve grown less patient when it comes to grinding for better glyphs.</li>
<li>The PSP remake of <em>Rondo of Blood</em>, <a href="https://jefklakscodex.com/games/psp/castlevania-dracula-x-chronicles/">Dracula X Chronicles</a>, is mostly a good excuse to play the original, if you manage to unlock it.</li>
</ul>
<p>Most of the gaming evenings were spent chasing after Diablo and murdering his Prime Evil brethren in <a href="https://jefklakscodex.com/games/switch/diablo-2-resurrected/">Diablo II: Resurrected</a>. I played the Switch port and wouldn&rsquo;t recommend it unless you don&rsquo;t own decent hardware like I do. After a few cow runs, I got tired of it&mdash;yet again, <em>the grind</em> fatigue hits me. The only unique item I saw drop was a flail my warlock couldn&rsquo;t even use.</p>
<h2 id="selected-blog-posts">Selected (blog) posts</h2>
<ul>
<li>Jaap-Henk Hoepman&rsquo;s <a href="https://blog.xot.nl/2026/09/29/it-s-not-the-super-intelligence-stupid/index.html">stance on genAI</a> mirrors mine. Academia is fucked as well, it seems.</li>
<li>The <a href="https://nabiu.studio/garden">Naibu Studio Garden website</a> is beautiful. The blueberry tracking your mouse is a nice touch.</li>
<li>In case you&rsquo;re in dire need of a <a href="https://mapped.earth/lighthouses/world">world map of lighthouses</a>, Aaron J. Becker has got you covered. I discovered there are a couple of floating lighthouses between Belgium and the UK with sweeping beams:</li>
</ul>
